{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Bereshit.</b> Therefore the Torah began with the letter bet, because the world resembles a bet, which is enclosed on three of its sides and the north side is not enclosed. And at that time the letter alef came and lodged a complaint, and the Holy One, blessed be He, repaid it at the giving of the Torah, for He opened with the alef of 'Anokhi.' And in the word 'bereshit' there are six letters, corresponding to the six days of creation. And in that verse there are seven words, corresponding to the days of the week. And in it, twenty-eight letters, corresponding to the twenty-eight days of the month. And in this verse there are six alefs, corresponding to the six thousand years of the existence of the world, for each and every alef denotes a thousand. And in the verse following it, 'veha'aretz,' he wrote two alefs, corresponding to the two thousand years of the days of the Messiah. And in the portion 'Bo,' at the verse 'למען תהיה תורת ה׳ בפיך,' he wrote two alefs, corresponding to the two thousand [years] of Torah." "<b>Bereshit.</b> Rashi explained: for the merit of the Torah, which is called 'reshit,' and likewise you find the merit of Sabbath, covenant, and circumcision — and it is derived from them, for in the word 'bereshit' you will find 'shabbat,' 'berit,' 'esh,' and the Torah was likened to fire, as it is written: ״אש דת למו״. And Rashi further explained the saying of Rabbi Yitzchak: 'He did not need to begin the Torah' etc. And it is difficult, for were they not already commanded concerning circumcision and the sinew of the thigh? However, one may say that he cited the first commandment with which all Israel were commanded together, and not an individual."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:15:32.324048898Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}